{
  "dom_id": "step-q108088",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "$\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\sqrt[5]{10})=$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite $\\sqrt[5]{10}$ as a power of $10$ (the base of the common logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[5]{10}={10}^{1/5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\sqrt[5]{10})=\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{1/5})\n$$\n\nThe common logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The principle is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x})=x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $x=\\frac{1}{5}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{1/5})=\\frac{1}{5}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
